From d07a49bd0cc9783a46371887789c21e1ae457053 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marc <marc@schuetze.io>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 23:50:24 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 17/19] screamer: read guest audio at the sample rate

The device copied its whole host buffer (2049 frames) from guest memory in
one burst. Mac OS X keeps a safety margin of 45 frames, so the copy ran ahead
of what CoreAudio had written and silence was played: 25 % of the audible
time of a work was lost, with gaps on a 2049 frame grid.

Pace the TX channel with the virtual clock, at most 1 ms per step, and buffer
on the host side behind the read. Descriptor completion, interrupts and the
frame counter now share one timeline; the frame counter is writable.
